SUMMARY:Crane's Mill:  The Story Behind the Name
DESCRIPTION:Join local historian Bob Williams on Tuesday\, October 13 at 
 6:30 p.m. at the West Caldwell Public Library for a fascinating look at the 
 history of Crane’s Mill and its connection to West Caldwell.\n\nThe story 
 has a personal connection for Williams. When he was just 15 years old\, he 
 purchased a collection of historic ledgers from Crane’s Sawmill in West 
 Caldwell. By then\, the mill had already been dismantled and moved to 
 Allaire Village in South Jersey for reconstruction although it was never 
 rebuilt. The mill’s foundation ruins remained in West Caldwell for 
 years\, becoming a favorite place for Williams to explore throughout his 
 youth and into adulthood.
LOCATION:West Caldwell - Community Meeting Room\, West Caldwell Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="West Caldwell Public Library":MAILTO:programs@westcaldwell.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10340-17459708
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17459708
