SUMMARY:Morning Book Club
DESCRIPTION: The Color Of Water by James McBride\n\nWho is Ruth McBride 
 Jordan? A self-declared "light-skinned" woman evasive about her ethnicity\, 
 yet steadfast in her love for her twelve black children. James McBride\, 
 journalist\, musician\, and son\, explores his mother's past\, as well as 
 his own upbringing and heritage\, in a poignant and powerful debut\, The 
 Color Of Water: A Black Man's Tribute to His White Mother.
