SUMMARY:Affordable College Solutions NOW ON ZOOM
DESCRIPTION:Register HERE\n\nJoin us for the special ZOOM presentation of 
 the "Cracking the Code: Affordable College Solutions" seminar.  \n\nIt 
 doesn't matter how old your kids are...now is the time to learn how to 
 finance college!\n\nThis program will be presented by a nationally 
 recognized Certified College Funding Specialist who has\nbeen invited to 
 speak to families and professionals by more than 65 organizations 
 nationwide. She has also\nprovided continuing education to over 40\,000 
 CPAs across the country on strategies to help make college\nmore 
 affordable.\nDesigned for parents with children of all ages—from newborn 
 through college—this engaging and informative\nsession addresses one of 
 the most stressful financial challenges families face today: how to pay for 
 college\nwithout jeopardizing long-term financial goals and retirement. 
 Even higher-income families with substantial\nresources can feel 
 overwhelmed by the tremendous cost of school and seek guidance to navigate 
 the quickly\nevolving college process to secure discounts and preserve 
 their wealth.\nA featured focus of the presentation is recent legislation 
 often referred to as “The Big Beautiful Bill\,” and\nwhat it means for 
 college savings\, financial aid\, and affordability. The presenter will 
 explain these changes in a\nclear\, practical\, and easy-to-understand 
 way.\nParticipants will also learn about:\n● How to secure a quality 
 education without overpaying for college\n● Understanding the financial 
 aid landscape: FAFSA and CSS Profiles\, need-based and merit-based 
 aid\,\nathletic and private scholarships\n● Student Aid Index (SAI): How 
 it’s calculated and directly impacts your family’s financial aid 
 eligibility\n● Pros and Cons of Diverse College Savings Vehicles - a look 
 at 529 plans as well as alternative savings\nstrategies and determining how 
 to choose what’s right for your family\n● How to reduce student loan 
 debt and plan for repayment without sacrificing your family’s future\n● 
 Strategies to recapture out-of-pocket college expenses\n● Positioning 
 families to maximize college discounts: Practical strategies—even for 
 higher-income\nhouseholds—to unlock savings opportunities\nParticipants 
 will gain valuable insights\, expert guidance\, and creative strategies to 
 help make smarter college\nfunding decisions while protecting the ability 
 to retire comfortably. This program is designed to simplify and\ndemystify 
 the college funding process\, empowering families to reduce costs and avoid 
 unnecessary debt.\nWhether your child was just born or is approaching 
 college decisions\, this program will provide clarity\,\nconfidence\, and 
 practical guidance you can use right away.\n\n\n\nPRESENTED BY: Jodi 
 Bloom\, MBA\nCertified College Funding Specialist\nFounder and College 
 Planning Expert\n\n161 Madison Avenue\nSuite 230\nMorristown\, NJ 
 07960\nPhone: 201-463-3024\nwebsite www.myccws.com\nEmail: jodi@myccws.com
LOCATION:West Caldwell - Zoom
ORGANIZER;CN="West Caldwell Public Library":MAILTO:programs@westcaldwell.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture, Live Stream
UID:LibCal-10340-17265901
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17265901
END:VEVENT
